<h2 id="glossary">Glossary</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Edge AI</strong> — inference on local devices near the data source</li>
<li><strong>Cloud AI</strong> — inference in remote datacenters</li>
<li><strong>Data gravity</strong> — tendency of large datasets to pull compute toward them</li>
<li><strong>p99 latency</strong> — 99th-percentile latency; tail behavior</li>
<li><strong>Early exit</strong> — network heads allowing easy inputs to finish early</li>
<li><strong>Cascade</strong> — small model filters, big model handles hard cases</li>
<li><strong>Split inference</strong> — part of the network on-device, part in cloud</li>
<li><strong>Federated learning</strong> — training across devices without centralizing data</li>
<li><strong>Non-IID</strong> — data differing across clients, harming federated convergence</li>
<li><strong>Cold start</strong> — first-request latency penalty in serverless cloud</li>
<li><strong>Crossover point</strong> — volume where edge and cloud costs equalize</li>
<li><strong>Degraded mode</strong> — reduced functionality during disconnection</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2 id="practice-exercises">Practice Exercises</h2>
<ol>
<li>Decompose cloud inference latency into four components and explain which dominates for a voice assistant.</li>
<li>A camera generates 150 GB/day. Compute the monthly cloud transfer cost at $0.09/GB and compare with a $120 edge device amortized over 3 years.</li>
<li>Explain data gravity with a concrete example from your field.</li>
<li>Design a hierarchical cascade for a wildlife camera. State the threshold tuning method and what curve you would plot.</li>
<li>Why must energy comparisons include the radio? Give numbers for an LTE upload vs on-device inference.</li>
<li>Sketch the capex/opex crossover model for a 1,000-sensor deployment. What are the three most sensitive assumptions?</li>
<li>Describe a privacy boundary for a health-sensing app: what crosses it, in what form, and why?</li>
<li>Design a placement experiment matrix for your own task: conditions, controls, metrics.</li>
<li>Explain the non-IID problem in federated learning and how you would demonstrate it experimentally.</li>
<li>Write the abstract (150 words) of a placement paper for your task, including the decision rule.</li>
</ol>
